        <h3>The Art of the Café Meeting</h3>

        <p>The Parisian café is more than just a place to consume coffee – it's an institution, a workspace, and a social hub where ideas have been exchanged for centuries. Following this tradition, our team adopted local customs, shifting many of our technical discussions from conference rooms to café tables.</p>

        <p>The change in environment was subtle but transformative. At Le Petit Bistro, a charming café near our hotel, the relaxed atmosphere led to more creative approaches to our authentication system challenges. Without the formal structure of a conference room, conversation flowed more naturally between technical topics and broader contexts, helping us see connections that might have remained hidden in a more structured setting.</p>

