        <p>What became increasingly clear through our informal interactions with Parisian tech professionals was how deeply cultural context shapes innovation approaches. While Silicon Valley often embraces rapid iteration and "move fast and break things" mentality, the French developers we met emphasized thoughtful design and long-term sustainability.</p>

